return function(require)
-- Standard ability level-up orders. Slots: 0=Q 1=W 2=E 3=R.
-- first = order in which each basic ability gets its first point (levels 1-3);
-- max   = priority for maxing basics after that; r = levels at which R is taken ({} = never levelled).
-- seq   = the raw source letters, kept so each derivation can be audited.
--
-- Normal rows: lolalytics.com highest-win-rate "Skill Order" table (levels 1-15) for the most-played lane,
-- site patch label 16.20 (= live 26.20), read 2026-10-10. The table stops at level 15, so the third R rank is 16.
-- R is listed at its earliest legal levels 6/11/16; occasional delays to 12 in a table (Caitlyn, Corki,
-- Twisted Fate) are not reproduced. Small samples are marked in a note.
--
-- Classic rows: metasrc.com League Classic build pages (patch 26.20, 18-level grid), read 2026-10-10.
-- A Classic row exists only where metasrc lists the champion in its Classic roster; otherwise it is omitted (the
-- driver then uses the Normal order for a Classic kit only when `classicSameKit=true`). No row sets
-- classicSameKit: every champion without a Classic row is also absent from the metasrc Classic roster
-- (Jhin, Jinx, Rell, Seraphine, Thresh, Viktor, Xerath, Yone, Yunara, Zed), so kit equivalence is unverified.
-- These are community statistics, not verified mechanics; the driver must still check level-up legality live.
